  <revision rev="7" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>daf0cacdb9553c7dce643c545b889854</srcmd5>
    <version>0.6.1</version>
    <time>1785705223</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Allow installing corrosion alongside rustup

The rustup package ships /usr/bin/cargo and /usr/bin/rustc itself and
conflicts with the cargo and rust packages, without providing those
capabilities. The hard &quot;Requires: cargo&quot; and &quot;Requires: rust&quot; can therefore
only be satisfied by the distro toolchain, so rustup users cannot install
corrosion at all -- zypper offers only &quot;deinstall rustup&quot; or &quot;break the
dependency&quot;. Note that the cargo package's own description recommends rustup
for development systems.

Rich dependencies keep the distro-toolchain case unchanged and additionally
accept rustup. Nothing is lost: since 0.6.0 dropped the native tooling,
corrosion ships only CMake files and calls whatever cargo/rustc are on PATH.

Build results are unchanged from the devel package (SLE_12 and 15.7 were
already unresolvable), and the resulting rpm installs cleanly against
rustup 1.28.2 on Tumbleweed.

This affects anyone building KDE from source with rustup: current KDE master
calls find_package(Corrosion) in five modules. (forwarded request 1368822 from dfaure)</comment>
    <requestid>1368873</requestid>
  </revision>
